oth whole trees and subtrees of the SAME tree, e.g. test_merge_recovery.py walks SRC.rglob('*.py') while store/test_git_outcome.py walks (SRC/'_store').rglob and store/test_store_paths.py walks _SRC_REBAR.rglob; reconciler tests walk _REC/_ADAPTERS/_REDUCER; test_review_discovery_architecture.py walks _LLM. Files under _store/_REC/_LLM are re-parsed by both the subtree scan and the src/rebar whole-tree scan under a per-root key.","The prototype the plan leans on (tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py `@functools.cache def _parsed(path)`) is itself PER-FILE, memoising by path so overlapping walks collapse to one parse per file regardless of root."],"finding":"The plan chose a per-ROOT parse cache (functools.cache keyed on root.resolve()) but the redundancy it targets spans NESTED roots that a per-root key cannot collapse; a per-FILE cache (the shape of the existing in-repo prototype it cites) would share more work and is not considered or ruled out.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd596658b2cd60bf0","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / 'parsed_python_files(root) ... cached via functools.cache with the root .resolve()'","norm_id":"n6c8cbd2b7892687e","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A single-process run of the migrated set where one scanner walks src/rebar and another walks src/rebar/_store: every _store file is parsed twice under the per-root design but once under a per-file design.","Reconciler subtree scanners (_REC, _ADAPTERS) co-running with a whole src/rebar scanner."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Consider memoising ast.parse per resolved FILE path (walk the root, then map each *.py through a `@functools.cache` per-file parse) rather than caching by root; this collapses redundancy across the many nested roots the suite actually walks (src/rebar vs _store/_REC/_LLM subtrees) and matches the validated in-repo prototype, at the cost of the per-file cache not carrying the whole-tree filter 